let's get the latest information tonight  from dr anthony fauci of the national  institutes of allergy and infectious  disease dr fauci always good to see you  so  as phil mentioned phase three trials of  the new moderna vaccine began  6 45 this morning with the first of 30  000 patients getting  what will be one of two shots 28 days  apart what will you be looking for  during these phase three trials well the  the phase three  charles john is that the major uh  question  is does it work it isn't effective and  that's exactly what we're looking for  obviously  you want to look for safety concerns  also but the main  issue here is you vaccinate  15 000 people will get the vaccine 15  000 will get a placebo and then you  determine  the difference in infection with the  coronavirus  in each of those groups so it's a  two-ohm study as you said  correctly it's a prime followed by a  boost  28 days later and hopefully within a  period  of a few months we'll be able to get a  signal to know whether it actually is  effective  in preventing infection with the  coronavirus it's it's extraordinary  circumstance john because this is the  fastest  that we have ever gone from the  identification of a new virus  doing the sequence getting a vaccine and  going into a phase three trial for  efficacy  and we've done it by increased  technologies that have really been  transforming the way we do vaccine  trials well necessity is the mother of  all invention based on the initial data  dr fatchi how optimistic are you that  you will get what you're looking for  from this modern vaccine  you know john if you look at the the  results from the phase one trial albeit  a relatively small number of individuals  the vaccine induced in those individuals  a level of antibody neutralizing  antibody which is the  hallmark of protection at levels that  were at least  as good and in some cases better than  what you would see  from people who were convalescing from  natural infection  so even though the numbers of people  were small the fact that you can induce  a response  that mimics what you do with natural  infection  is good news so that makes me cautiously  optimistic  that we may have something here but it's  going to take a few months  to determine whether or not we do in the  early days of the vaccine development dr  fauci you laid out that the  the government was going to do things  differently here that it was going to  proactively start to  build up a supply the president talked  about that  earlier today let's listen what he said  we're mass producing all of the most  promising vaccine candidates in advance  so that on the day one that it's  approved  it'll be available to the american  people immediately and we'll probably  have a lot for a lot of other people  throughout the world the world is  suffering from this  giant virus as we mentioned that that's  a departure from the way that things  normally go you usually don't scale up  until after  phase three trials are over and then  you've got that six month lag so that  will get it out there  quickly but a lot of people have a  question as to  who will get it first right it's a good  question john and what we're going to do  is we're going to take that very  seriously  there are committees that are formed to  make a recommendation  of getting the vaccine out equitably to  the people  who would benefit from it most and that  is not something that you take lightly  so what will happen  is that there will be a prioritization  hopefully as we get into 2021 john  we'll have enough vaccine for everyone  who needs it but early on  when you first start distributing it  we're not going to have  everything for everyone sure what you'll  do is probably have people  who could benefit the most and those who  are most vulnerable for example  first responders the people are going to  be putting themselves at risk  taking care of patients with covert 19  those who are vulnerable the elderly  those with underlying conditions  because we know now from sad experience  that individuals have underlying  conditions are much more likely  to have a serious negative outcome from  infection  president trump talked the other day  about potentially having people get the  first shots in september maybe october  which has led some people to say oh is  this going to be an october surprise in  the political campaign  here's what the secretary of hhs alex  azar said about that earlier  there's no politics in any of this we  need therapeutics and we need vaccines  and we need them as quickly as we can  get them  and we are working to mit to basically  shave every day off the development and  manufacturing that we can do  that we can that we can do so and but  we're going to make sure that any  therapeutic or  any vaccine is safe and effective up to  the fda's  gold standards so dr fauci obviously you  want to get a vaccine out there as  quickly as possible  is there any political pressure to get  this out there before november the third  and  any are any corners being cut in order  to do that  well certainly there are no corners  being cut john i'll guarantee you that  safety is very important what we're  doing is not compromising safety  and certainly not compromising  scientific integrity  we in fact briefed the president today  about this  in the oval office and there is no  political pressure  that i've seen it all to move quickly  the the the speed of the trial  and how quickly you get the results is  dependent upon certain factors  one is the number of infections that you  get within the context of the trial  to determine if it works or not so if we  go out there we're going to have 30  000 people in the trial 15 000 will get  the  vaccine and 15 000 would be placebo if  you look at the accrual and the rate of  accrual  that you could project that you'll get  an answer sometime  in the mid to late fall that could be  november that could be october it's  very very difficult to predict it's  going to be  the infection rate and the people who  get vaccinated  are they within that group something we  can predict  dr fauci we've got about 30 seconds left  phil keating mentioned  that there has been the beginning of a  plateauing of some of the spike that  we've seen in states like texas  arizona and florida what do you think is  responsible for that  and does that bode well for not having  to roll back the reopening that we've  seen  well certainly you like to see when you  get surges like that which were very  disturbing john  that you begin to see them plateau that  means hopefully people are starting to  do the fundamental things  that we've been telling them to do about  mask wearing  avoiding crowds closing the bars  health you know hand hygiene etc  hopefully and i believe it is  now having an impact we've got to make  sure that other states  that are starting to show an uptick do  what we're talking about  before you get the major surge otherwise  we're going to be repeating what we saw  in some of those southern states  which would really be a shame if that  happens all right well everybody's got  to do their part we should mention you  know we  we talked with you last week about your  debut throwing out the first pitch  we've got a a frame of that at the  nationals park and we should also point  out  that you now have the top selling  baseball card in history  51 512 cards sold in 24 hours there's  the card from tops  50 years from now you could be the next  hoeness wagner we'll see  dr fauci great to see you thanks so much  great to see you john thanks

